cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  G4_Promoter_Pipeline: a Snakemake workflow for promoter-centric
  G-quadruplex and R-loop analysis of CUT&Tag and RNA-seq data
message: >-
  If you use this workflow, please cite it using the metadata in this file.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Daniel J.
    family-names: Goodall
    affiliation: Hubrecht Institute, Utrecht, The Netherlands
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5942-6303"
  - given-names: K.
    family-names: Sato
    affiliation: Hubrecht Institute, Utrecht, The Netherlands
  - given-names: P.
    family-names: Knipscheer
    affiliation: Hubrecht Institute, Utrecht, The Netherlands
repository-code: "https://github.com/DJ-Goodall/G4_Promoter_Pipeline"
abstract: >-
  A single reproducible Snakemake workflow that takes public G-quadruplex (BG4)
  and R-loop (S9.6) CUT&Tag coverage tracks together with an RNA-seq count table
  from wild-type, DHX36 knockout, FANCJ knockout and double-knockout mouse
  embryonic stem cells, and produces the complete analysis: RNA-seq quality
  control, differential expression and functional enrichment; replicate-aware
  CUT&Tag peak calling and genomic region building; genome-wide and regional
  signal enrichment; integration of differential expression with promoter and
  TSS occupancy; sequence-level G-quadruplex topology assignment combining
  pqsfinder, DeepG4 and G4ShapePredictor with literature-based calibration;
  topology-resolved metaprofiles across promoters, 5' UTRs, first introns,
  enhancers and lncRNAs; G-quadruplex versus R-loop coupling; multi-G4 promoter
  analysis at motif resolution; and strand-asymmetry plus locus-level track
  visualisation. Fifty numbered scripts are wired into roughly fifty Snakemake
  rules, all parameters live in a single configuration file, and every
  intermediate is cached so the workflow reproduces end to end from public data.
keywords:
  - G-quadruplex
  - R-loop
  - CUT&Tag
  - RNA-seq
  - Snakemake
  - reproducible workflow
  - DHX36
  - FANCJ
  - promoter
  - transcription
  - mouse embryonic stem cells
  - mm10
  - bioinformatics
license: MIT
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-07-30"
